} Workspace object: Field Type Description id integer Unique workspace identifier name string Name of the workspace owner User Owner of the workspace member_count integer Number of members in the workspace handle string Workspace handle (e.g., domain or identifier like otter.ai) type string Type of workspace (e.g., business) Error responses: Status Description 404 User not in a workspace GET /workspace/{id}/analytics Use this endpoint to retrieve workspace usage analytics for a date range, including total transcribed minutes, conversation counts, current license counts, and per-member usage sorted by name. Operation ID: getWorkspaceAnalytics Base URL: https://api.otter.ai/v1 Path Parameters: Parameter Type Required Description id string Yes Workspace ID. Use GET /workspace to retrieve your workspace details, including its ID. Query Parameters: Parameter Type Required Description start_date string (date) No Inclusive start date in yyyy-mm-dd format. Omit together with end_date to use the last 30 days. If only start_date is provided, the end of the range defaults to now. end_date string (date) No Inclusive end date in yyyy-mm-dd format. Cannot be provided without start_date . timezone string No IANA timezone used to interpret dates, such as America/Los_Angeles . Defaults to the workspace timezone, then America/Los_Angeles . Date range behavior: Omit both dates to retrieve analytics for the last 30 days. Provide only start_date to use now as the end of the range. Providing only end_date is invalid. When both dates are provided, the range is inclusive, from 00:00:00 on the start date through 23:59:59 on the end date in the resolved timezone. Note: num_of_minutes , num_of_conversations , and members are scoped to the resolved report window. seats_used and seats_invoiced are current license counts and are not historical values for the report window. Example Request: curl -X GET "https://api.otter.ai/v1/workspace/{id}/analytics?start_date=2026-09-01&end_date=2026-09-30&timezone=America%2FLos_Angeles" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY" Replace {id} with your workspace ID. This GET request has no request body. Response: A successful request returns 200 OK with content type application/json and a WorkspaceAnalyticsResponse . meta : Response metadata, including retrieved_at data : The workspace analytics object for the resolved date range The following example uses illustrative values. {
  "meta": {
    "retrieved_at": "2026-10-01T12:00:00Z"
  },
  "data": {
    "start_date": "2026-09-01",
    "end_date": "2026-09-30",
    "timezone": "America/Los_Angeles",
    "num_of_minutes": 120,
    "num_of_conversations": 4,
    "seats_used": 1,
    "seats_invoiced": 5,
    "members": [
      {
        "id": "hashed_user_id",
        "name": "Jane Doe",
        "email": "jane@example.com",
        "status": "Activated",
        "num_of_conversations": 4,
        "num_of_minutes": 120,
        "average_conversations_per_month": 4,
        "average_minutes_per_conversation": 30,
        "average_minutes_per_month": 120,
        "join_date": "2026-08-15",
        "last_activity_at": "2026-09-30T18:30:00Z",
        "last_login_at": "2026-09-30T16:00:00Z",
        "num_of_ai_chats": 2,
        "num_of_conversations_shared_by_user": 2,
        "num_of_conversations_shared_with_user": 0,
        "num_of_conversations_viewed": 4
      }
    ]
  }
} Response fields: Field Type Required Description meta object (CommonMeta) Yes Response metadata. meta.retrieved_at string (date-time) Yes Timestamp when the data was retrieved (ISO 8601 format). data object (WorkspaceAnalytics) Yes Workspace analytics for the resolved report window. Workspace analytics object: Field Type Required Description start_date string (date) Yes Resolved inclusive start date of the report window ( yyyy-mm-dd ). end_date string (date) Yes Resolved inclusive end date of the report window ( yyyy-mm-dd ). timezone string Yes IANA timezone used to interpret dates. Defaults to the workspace timezone, then America/Los_Angeles . num_of_minutes number Yes Total transcribed minutes for workspace members in the report window. num_of_conversations number Yes Total conversations created by workspace members in the report window. seats_used integer Yes Current licensed seats in use. Not scoped to the report window. seats_invoiced integer Yes Current invoiced seat quantity. Not scoped to the report window. members array of WorkspaceAnalyticsMember objects Yes Per-member usage for the report window, sorted by name. Workspace analytics member object: Field Type Required Description id string Yes Opaque hashed user ID. name string Yes Member name. email string (email) Yes Member email address. status string Yes Member status: Activated , Deactivated , or Pending . num_of_conversations number Yes Conversations created by this member in the report window. num_of_minutes number Yes Minutes transcribed by this member in the report window. average_conversations_per_month number Yes Average number of conversations per month. average_minutes_per_conversation number Yes Average transcribed minutes per conversation. average_minutes_per_month number Yes Average transcribed minutes per month. join_date string (date) or null No Member join date in the report timezone, or null if unknown. last_activity_at string (date-time) or null No Most recent conversation creation, conversation view, or annotation timestamp, or null if none. last_login_at string (date-time) or null No Most recent login timestamp, or null if the member has never logged in. num_of_ai_chats number or null No AI chats created by this member in the report window, or null if unavailable. num_of_conversations_shared_by_user number or null No Conversations shared by this member in the report window, or null if unavailable. num_of_conversations_shared_with_user number or null No Conversations shared with this member in the report window, or null if unavailable. num_of_conversations_viewed number or null No Conversations viewed by this member in the report window, or null if unavailable. Error responses: Status Description 400 Bad Request Invalid date range, timezone, or workspace ID. This includes providing end_date without start_date . 403 Forbidden Caller is not a workspace admin. 404 Not Found Workspace not found. Errors use content type application/json and an ErrorResponse object containing a required errors array. The response schemas are ValidationErrorResponse (400), ForbiddenErrorResponse (403), and NotFoundErrorResponse (404). Error response fields: Field Type Required Description errors array of RequestError objects Yes Details about the request errors. errors[].status string No HTTP error status text. errors[].code string No Specific error code defined by Otter. errors[].detail string No Description of the error. errors[].source object (RequestErrorSource) No Information about the request source. May be null , as shown in the example below. errors[].source.header string No Header information associated with the error. errors[].source.parameter string No Request parameter information associated with the error. errors[].source.pointer string (URI) No URI identifying the request source associated with the error. Example Error Response (403): {
  "errors": [
    {
      "status": "Forbidden",
      "code": "403",
      "detail": "User has no permission",
      "source": null
    }
  ]
} 👉 Best Practices Rate Limiting Implement appropriate rate limiting in your application to avoid overwhelming the API. Consider implementing exponential backoff for retries. Error Handling Always check for and handle error responses gracefully. Parse the error details to provide meaningful feedback to users. Pagination Use cursor-based pagination for large result sets. Don't attempt to retrieve all data in a single request. Selective Loading Use the include parameter in conversation endpoints to fetch only the data you need. This reduces response payload size and improves performance. Caching Cache responses where appropriate to reduce API calls. Consider implementing a caching layer for frequently accessed data. Field Selection When using the include parameter, only request the fields you actually need rather than using all Related to api Related articles Workspace Webhooks Does Otter offer an open API? Custom Meeting Type Templates HIPAA | Otter.ai Set a custom Data Retention policy Article is closed for comments. ✨ On this page ↑ Back to top × ❮ ❯

